    <statement><p><m>32.94</m> grams of pure alcohol was used to produce a bottle of <m>12.2\%</m> alcohol solution. What is the weight of the solution in grams?</p>
<p>The alcohol solution weighs <fillin characters="9" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>270\ {\rm g}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>This problem can be boiled down to this question: <m>32.94</m> is <m>12.2\%</m> of what? We will show multiple methods to solve this problem.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 1</p>
<p>We will use proportion to solve this problem. Assume <m>32.94</m> is <m>12.2\%</m> of <m>x</m>, so <lq/><m>12.2</m> out of <m>100</m><rq/> corresponds to <lq/><m>32.94</m> out of <m>x</m><rq/>.</p>
<p>We will write and solve the proportion:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}[t]
   \frac{12.2}{100} \amp = \frac{32.94}{x} \\
   12.2x \amp = 100 \cdot 32.94 \\
   12.2x \amp = 3294 \\
   \frac{12.2x}{12.2} \amp = \frac{3294}{12.2} \\
   x \amp = 270
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>The alcohol solution weighs <m>{270\ {\rm g}}</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 2</p>
<p>We will use the percentage formula to solve this problem. This translation from English to math may help you remember the percentage formula.</p>
<p><m>2 \text{ is } 50\% \text{ of } 4 \iff 2 = 0.5 \cdot 4</m></p>
<p>The question is: <m>32.94</m> is <m>12.2\%</m> of what? Assume <m>32.94</m> is <m>12.2\%</m> of <m>x</m>. We have:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}
        32.94  \amp  = 0.122 \cdot x \\
        \frac{32.94}{0.122} \amp  = \frac{0.122x}{0.122} \\
        270 \amp = x
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>The alcohol solution weighs <m>{270\ {\rm g}}</m>.</p>
<!-- PTX:WARNING: PGML wanted to make this a level 4 header. -->
<p>
Method 3</p>
<p>In the sentence <lq/><m>32.94</m> is <m>12.2\%</m> of what,<rq/></p>
<p><ul label="disc">
<li>
<p><m>32.94</m> is the <alert>percentage</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>12.2\%</m> is the <alert>rate</alert>,</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><lq/>what<rq/> is the <alert>base</alert> (following the word <lq/>of<rq/>).</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p>By the formula <m>\text{base} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{rate}}</m>, we do a division to solve the problem:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ \text{base} = \frac{\text{percentage}}{\text{rate}} = \frac{32.94}{12.2\%} = \frac{32.94}{0.122} = 270 }</m></p>
<p>The alcohol solution weighs <m>{270\ {\rm g}}</m>.</p>
</solution>
